dsymutil --update cannot recompute the relocation map of a mergeable library,
as the dSYM holds final addresses and no relocations. Check that it keeps the
map of the dSYM, when updating it into a new bundle, onto itself, or in place.

RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
RUN: dsymutil -oso-prepend-path=%p/.. \
RUN:   %p/../Inputs/mergeable-libs/dwarf5/libfoo.dylib -o %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: cp %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM/Contents/Resources/Relocations/aarch64/libfoo.dylib.yml \
RUN:   %t/map.yml

RUN: dsymutil --update %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM -o %t/updated.dSYM
RUN: diff %t/map.yml \
RUN:   %t/updated.dSYM/Contents/Resources/Relocations/aarch64/libfoo.dylib.yml

RUN: dsymutil --update %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM -o %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: diff %t/map.yml \
RUN:   %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM/Contents/Resources/Relocations/aarch64/libfoo.dylib.yml

RUN: dsymutil --update %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM
RUN: diff %t/map.yml \
RUN:   %t/libfoo.dylib.dSYM/Contents/Resources/Relocations/aarch64/libfoo.dylib.yml
